Session notes: proxy to plugin

Why
---
Claude Code shipped function hooks (anthropics/claude-code#91870), which
put a TypeScript middleware chain inside the engine. That makes the CA
MITM proxy unnecessary for Claude Code: the same substitution can happen
at the tool boundary, with no certificate, no listener and no daemon.

What was studied
----------------
- The Mods announcement and the three built-in mods published at
  anthropics/claude-code/tree/main/mods (sec-default, diff, telemetry).
- mods/types/claude-code.d.ts, the engine declaration file, vendored here
  as types/claude-code.d.ts.
- The community secret-redactor plugin, which uses opaque placeholders.
  osm keeps format-preserving fakes instead, so the model still reasons
  about the value as a credential of that vendor.

Design decisions
----------------
- Session-scoped in-memory vault instead of the encrypted SQLite store.
  A proxy daemon outlived many sessions and needed persistence. A plugin
  does not, so the crypto and passphrase layers were dropped entirely.
- tool.call is the single interception point in both directions. It
  covers every built-in tool and every MCP tool without naming any.
- Hooks catch their own errors. The engine skips a throwing hook and runs
  core in its place, which for a masking hook is worse than absence.
- A rewritten tool result answers without ref, because ref names the
  messages core already built from the unmasked content.
- Math.random is enough for garble, because the fake is sent to the model
  by design and is therefore public.

Testing
-------
Two runners, both driving a real model.
- scripts/local-e2e.sh: a local account, Claude Code 2.1.272.
- scripts/sandbox-e2e.sh: a disposable Linux box via the CreateOS driver,
  Claude Code upgraded from 2.1.260 to 2.1.272, wired to OpenRouter over
  the Anthropic wire (base URL openrouter.ai/api with no /v1, bearer
  token, every model alias pinned, IS_SANDBOX=1).

Each runner does a control pass with no plugin, so a pass proves the
fixture is readable rather than proving nothing. Both runners passed.

Traps found while writing the runners
-------------------------------------
- --allowedTools is variadic, so a prompt after it is parsed as a tool
  name. Pass the prompt on stdin.
- A prompt that asks the model to write a credential to a file is refused
  as an exfiltration pattern. The restore direction is observed with
  grep -c instead.
- The Read tool needs explicit approval for a .env file.
- claude --plugin-dir takes the directory holding .claude-plugin, so
  running it from inside the clone needs a plain dot.

